{
  // Type-checks EVERY test and story file under `src/`, and emits nothing.
  //
  // `tsconfig.app.json` excludes `**/*.test.ts`, `**/*.test.tsx` and
  // `**/*.stories.tsx`, so before this file existed NO web test or story file
  // was type-checked by anything. `pnpm test` runs through vitest/esbuild,
  // which strips types without checking them. That is issue #340: a required
  // argument added to a source file is enforced at every source call site and
  // at none of the test call sites.
  //
  // Why a separate config and NOT a wider `include` in `tsconfig.app.json`:
  // that config is the one `tsc -b` builds. Adding these files to it would put
  // test code in the build graph. `apps/server/tsconfig.scripts.json` carries
  // the same note for the same reason. **Do not merge the two.**
  //
  // THE TWO PASSES OVERLAP HERE, unlike `apps/server`'s. Test files import
  // from `src`, so TypeScript pulls those source files into this program and
  // checks them a second time. The cost is recorded in the root CLAUDE.md.
  //
  // **`exclude` IS EMPTY. All 358 test and story files are checked.** Issue
  // #340 step 3 emptied the backlog in three waves: 405 errors in 6 files,
  // then 149 in 14, then 172 in 72 plus 22 collateral smoke tests and 2 in
  // the invisible file described in trap (d). Putting a file back on that
  // list re-opens the backlog — fix the test instead.
  //
  // **`"exclude": []` MUST STAY. DELETING THE KEY IS NOT THE SAME THING.**
  // `exclude` is inherited through `extends`, and `tsconfig.app.json:38` is
  // `"exclude": ["**/*.test.ts", "**/*.test.tsx", "**/*.stories.tsx"]` — the
  // very files this config exists to check. Measured 2026-10-30: with the key
  // deleted, `tsc --listFiles` finds **1** test or story file instead of 358
  // (the one named in `files`, which `exclude` cannot remove) and reports
  // **1** error instead of 0. A near-zero error count here is a broken
  // config, not a clean tree.
  //
  // THREE THINGS IN `include` THAT ARE NOT OBVIOUS, each measured:
  //
  // 1. `src/main.tsx` holds the TanStack Router `Register` interface
  //    augmentation (main.tsx:51). Without it in the program, every
  //    `navigate({ search: (prev) => … })` callback loses its type and reports
  //    TS7006 `Parameter 'prev' implicitly has an 'any' type` — in SOURCE
  //    files, which are clean under `tsconfig.app.json`. Measured: 4 such
  //    errors in `src/routes/cooking.tsx` and 2 in
  //    `src/components/recipe/CookingControlBar/CookingControlBar.tsx`.
  //
  // 2. `src/test` holds `setup.ts`, whose first line is
  //    `import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest'`. That import is what
  //    declares `toBeInTheDocument`, `toHaveTextContent` and the rest on
  //    vitest's `Assertion`. No test file imports it — vitest loads it through
  //    `setupFiles` — so without `src/test` in the program the matchers are
  //    unknown. Measured: 1704 extra errors across 235 files.
  //
  // 3. `vitest/globals` in `types`, because `vitest.config.ts` sets
  //    `globals: true`, so `describe` / `it` / `expect` / `vi` are ambient.
  //
  // WHY THERE IS A `files` ENTRY FOR ONE TEST FILE — trap (d) below.
  //
  // FOUR MEASUREMENT TRAPS, kept because each one cost time when it was hit:
  //
  // a. To measure a backlog here, copy this file and put the files you want
  //    held back into its `exclude`. Do NOT strip the comments with a regex
  //    on `//` — it eats the `/**/` inside `src/**/*.test.ts` and turns the
  //    include into `src*.test.ts`, which checks ZERO files and reports ONE
  //    error. A suspiciously small number is a broken probe, not good news.
  //    The same number also means the inherited-`exclude` mistake above, so
  //    check the FILE COUNT with `--listFiles`, not the error count.
  //
  // b. Put a probe config INSIDE the repo. One written to `/tmp` resolves
  //    `typeRoots` from `/tmp/node_modules/@types` and reports a single
  //    misleading `TS2688` before checking any file.
  //
  // c. `exclude` only removes a file from the program's ROOT set. A file that
  //    an INCLUDED file imports is still pulled in and still checked. 22 clean
  //    `*.stories.test.tsx` smoke tests sat on the old list for that reason
  //    alone: each calls `composeStories` on a `*.stories.tsx` that was
  //    excluded, so excluding the story by itself left its errors reported
  //    against the smoke test. A pair has to move together, in both
  //    directions.
  //
  // d. `src/hooks/useItems.test.ts` and `src/hooks/useItems.test.tsx` both
  //    exist. TypeScript's `include` GLOB EXPANSION keeps only ONE file per
  //    path minus extension, and `.ts` wins, so `useItems.test.tsx` was
  //    INVISIBLE to this config — it reported 0 errors because it was in no
  //    program, not because it was clean. Emptying `exclude` does NOT fix
  //    that; the dedup is in the glob expansion, not in `exclude`. A `files`
  //    entry is not glob-expanded, so naming the `.tsx` there puts it in the
  //    root set alongside the `.ts`. Measured 2026-10-30: `tsc --listFiles`
  //    goes from 0 matches for the file to 1, and it then reported its own 2
  //    errors (`TS2550 Object.hasOwn`, `TS2532`), both now fixed.
  //    `git ls-files apps/web/src | grep -E '\.(test|stories)\.tsx?$' |
  //    sed -E 's/\.(ts|tsx)$//' | sort | uniq -d` lists every such collision.
  //    Today there is exactly one. Add a `files` entry for any new one.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // No `tsBuildInfoFile` and no `incremental`: this config is run with
    // `tsc -p`, not `tsc -b`, so it writes no build info and re-checks
    // everything on every run.
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["vite/client", "vite-plugin-pwa/client", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  // See trap (d). Glob expansion drops this file; a `files` entry does not.
  "files": ["src/hooks/useItems.test.tsx"],
  "include": [
    "src/main.tsx",
    "src/test",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/**/*.stories.tsx"
  ],
  // Empty ON PURPOSE, and not removable — see the note above. Without this
  // key the config inherits `tsconfig.app.json`'s exclude and checks 1 file.
  "exclude": []
}
